## Model routing

Choose for task quality first, then time, tokens and plan allowance; never compare API dollars across providers. First pick the rung the task needs for its shape and success signal; when torn between two adjacent rungs, take the higher.{{if .Both}} A meaningful task-fit advantage wins on either provider. Among sufficiently supported comparable routes, the Claude route is the reviewed default tie-break (a routing preference, not a claim of model superiority). About 2 index points, and for Implement, Fix and Verify Impl about 4 points on both FrontierCode 2.0 and Terminal-Bench 4.0, are comparison heuristics, not hard capability cutoffs. Check the evidence that matters for the task.{{end}} The declared plan allowance may reorder only comparable routes and never lowers the rung the task needs. Reroute once when evidence shows a route falls short. Effort names do not compare across models; use the ladder.

